>I had a failure of this on my local machine. I'm suspicious about this bit being called too soon

I think it is a correct guess. If task list is starting for a long time, something else could happen in a meanwhile. I was able to reproduce the failure with ~10% chance with:
```
Subject: [PATCH] format
---
Index: server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/action/admin/cluster/node/tasks/list/TransportListTasksAction.java
IDEA additional info:
Subsystem: com.intellij.openapi.diff.impl.patch.CharsetEP
<+>UTF-8
===================================================================
diff --git a/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/action/admin/cluster/node/tasks/list/TransportListTasksAction.java b/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/action/admin/cluster/node/tasks/list/TransportListTasksAction.java
--- a/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/action/admin/cluster/node/tasks/list/TransportListTasksAction.java	(revision dcb019dc15165d73c9145d632ef1fb23231b09dc)
+++ b/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/action/admin/cluster/node/tasks/list/TransportListTasksAction.java	(date 1704808639772)
@@ -94,6 +94,12 @@
     @Override
     protected void processTasks(CancellableTask nodeTask, ListTasksRequest request, ActionListener<List<Task>> nodeOperation) {
         if (request.getWaitForCompletion()) {
+            try {
+                Thread.sleep(500);
+            } catch (InterruptedException e) {
+                throw new RuntimeException(e);
+            }
+
             final ListenableActionFuture<List<Task>> future = new ListenableActionFuture<>();
             final List<Task> processedTasks = new ArrayList<>();
             final Set<Task> removedTasks = ConcurrentCollections.newConcurrentSet();
Index: server/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/action/admin/cluster/node/tasks/TasksIT.java
IDEA additional info:
Subsystem: com.intellij.openapi.diff.impl.patch.CharsetEP
<+>UTF-8
===================================================================
diff --git a/server/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/action/admin/cluster/node/tasks/TasksIT.java b/server/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/action/admin/cluster/node/tasks/TasksIT.java
--- a/server/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/action/admin/cluster/node/tasks/TasksIT.java	(revision dcb019dc15165d73c9145d632ef1fb23231b09dc)
+++ b/server/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/action/admin/cluster/node/tasks/TasksIT.java	(date 1704808639752)
@@ -600,10 +600,12 @@
                     @Override
                     public void onTaskUnregistered(Task task) {
                         waitForWaitingToStart.countDown();
+                        logger.info("--> Unregistered task {}", task);
                     }
                 });
             }
 
+            logger.info("--> Starting wait task");
             // Spin up a request to wait for the test task to finish
             waitResponseFuture = wait.apply(taskId);
 
@@ -611,6 +613,7 @@
              * reference to the running task. Because we unblock immediately after this the task may no longer be running for us to wait
              * on which is fine. */
             waitForWaitingToStart.await();
+            logger.info("--> Unblocking test task");
         } finally {
             // Unblock the request so the wait for completion request can finish
             client().execute(UNBLOCK_TASK_ACTION, new TestTaskPlugin.UnblockTestTasksRequest()).get();
```
in my case it was always caused by `internal:coordination/fault_detection/leader_check`, `internal:coordination/fault_detection/follower_check` but other tasks are also present.
